# Every file is checked out exactly as it was committed -- no line-ending
# conversion, on Windows or anywhere (v2026.11.342).
#
# Git on Windows, GitHub's Windows runners included, turns LF into CRLF on
# checkout by default. That broke two promises: the vendored readers in
# fme/vendor/ are meant to be byte-identical to what was published (their
# hashes are in fme/vendor/vendored.json), and `fme version` prints a
# fingerprint of the code so two examiners can tell they run the same
# program -- but the Windows build fingerprinted CRLF copies, so the same
# release gave one fingerprint from the .exe and another from source.
* -text
